Hi,

Here's the summary of today's IRC meeting.

---

COMMUNITY MEETING

Place: #openvpn-devel on irc.freenode.net
Date: Monday 9th Nov 2015
Time: 20:00 CET (19:00 UTC)

Planned meeting topics for this meeting were here:

<https://community.openvpn.net/openvpn/wiki/Topics-2015-11-09>

The next meeting has not been scheduled yet, but will probably be=20
arranged two weeks from now.

Your local meeting time is easy to check from services such as

<http://www.timeanddate.com/worldclock>

SUMMARY

cron2, lev, mattock, valdikss and syzzer participated in this meeting.

---

Discussed setting up a Flattr account for receiving donations. It was=20
agreed that it makes sense, but it was not clear who would take care of=20
the money, and how exactly the money would be distributed. Cron2=20
suggested using the money to sponsor the developer hackathons, which=20
have proven quite useful. Mattock will discuss this internally at the=20
company to see if the company could hold the money.


--

Discussed PolarSSL end-of-life, which is due on 31st December 2015.=20
Because very few package-based Linux distributions provide "OpenVPN with=20
PolarSSL" packages, we'll simply drop PolarSSL 1.2 support from OpenVPN=20
when the time comes. Source-based distributions probably don't have an=20
issue with us dropping PolarSSL 1.2 support, as their users can link to=20
1.3 easily at compile time.

--

Discussed setting up Travis-CI and Coverity for OpenVPN. It was agreed=20
that this is a good idea. Syzzer will do some testing in his own GitHub=20
fork of OpenVPN and when it works, we'll migrate the configuration to=20
the official GitHub repository.

--

Discussed the OpenVPN 2.3.9 release. The Windows 10 DNS fix from=20
valdikss should be included. ValdikSS will provide a separate patch for=20
2.3 and Git "master". We will aim at releasing 2.3.9 with PolarSSL 1.2=20
at the end of this month, and 2.3.10 with PolarSSL 1.3 about two weeks=20
after that.

--

Discussed the "=E2=80=8BUse adapter index instead of name" patch:

<http://article.gmane.org/gmane.network.openvpn.devel/10361>

Lev will look into the correct syntax for the interface definition and=20
get back.

--

Discussed the "=E2=80=8BSupport for disabled peer-id" patch:

<http://article.gmane.org/gmane.network.openvpn.devel/10216>

Syzzer promised to review this patch.

--

Discussed the "=E2=80=8BNotify clients about server's exit/restart" patch:

<http://thread.gmane.org/gmane.network.openvpn.devel/9496/focus=3D10278>

This has already been ACKed by Arne and will be merged soon.

--

Discussed the query username/password patches from dazo. Cron2 promised=20
to review them tomorrow evening.

--

Discussed the "When --disable is set for a client, the server never=20
replies to the client." ticket:

<https://community.openvpn.net/openvpn/ticket/521>

Mattock sent the reporter an email, asking him to test the patch dazo=20
had provided.

---

Full chatlog has been attached to this email.

--=20
Samuli Sepp=C3=A4nen
Community Manager
OpenVPN Technologies, Inc

irc freenode net: mattock

